// @emit-error index receiver is not an array or string
// THE DECLINE, pinned — because the alternative to declining here is a MISCOMPILE, and it was
// briefly shipped.
//
// `nested-array-inferred-empty-push.vl` covers the leaves the inferred-empty nested-array
// synthesis can type: i32, boolean, a literal union, string, f64, i64. This file pins what
// happens OUTSIDE that set, and the answer must stay a LOUD emit reject.
//
// WHY. The synthesis types the row from the arena (`arrLitNestedElemKind`), but the annotation
// it writes is resolved BY NAME, so the authority it has to agree with is
// `refArrElemKind(<elem> + "[]")`, and `rlInternName` keeps the FIRST kind banked for a rep key.
// The two agree on exactly the supported set. An `f32[]` leaf is kind 4 from the arena and kind
// 10 by name; a nested `i32[][]` leaf is 4 and 9. Either way the outer list's backing is typed as
// the i32-list wrapper while a different wrapper is stored into it — and the first version of
// that synthesis therefore turned this program's loud reject into `vl check` rc 0 plus a module
// that does not instantiate.
//
// Trading a loud reject for a silent miscompile is strictly worse than doing nothing, and the
// synthesis exists to close exactly that failure class. So the INTERN half declines every leaf
// outside the supported set, and that decline is what this file pins.
//
// THE TWO HALVES ARE NO LONGER ONE GATE (D625), AND THIS FILE IS THE CONTROL FOR THE SPLIT.
// The paragraph above used to end "so the uncovered leaves decline, in BOTH halves … because
// declining in only one reaches the same invalid module by the other route". The second half of
// that sentence was a prediction, and it was measured and refused: `nodeArrayElemName` (the
// ANNOTATION half) now asks the wider `tyNestedArrLeafRenders` — the element has a render — while
// `arrLitNestedElemName` (the INTERN half) keeps `tyNestedArrLeafSupported` exactly as it is.
//
// Nothing about THIS program moves, and that is the point: its `f32[]` leaf reaches the outer
// binding only through `.push`, with no declared destination anywhere in the module, so no
// earlier walk interned an `f32[][]` row for a synthesized annotation to resolve — and the same
// loud reject fires at the same position with the same message, byte for byte.
//
// What the widened half DOES reach is the case this file's leaf does not have: a declared
// destination that already interned the row. `function mkc(): f32[][] { const cc = []  return
// cc }` was `check-clean invalid wasm` and now runs, along with eight other leaves, pinned in
// `nested-array-inferred-empty-nested-ref-leaf.vl`. The old header claimed declining "keeps the
// LOUD reject master gives" for all of them; over a sixteen-leaf grid, NINE were silent.
//
// When a leaf here is genuinely supported, move it to a sibling fixture with an `@log`.
function f32Leaf() {
  const outer = []
  const inner: f32[] = [1.5, 2.5]
  outer.push(inner)
  print(outer[0][1])
}
f32Leaf()
